## Upgrading multiple nodes safely

When managing a multi-node cluster, upgrading all nodes in parallel risks losing etcd quorum. Use <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`dependsOn`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`DependsOn`" pulumi-lang-go="`dependsOn`" pulumi-lang-python="`depends_on`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`dependsOn`" pulumi-lang-java="`dependsOn`">`dependsOn`</span> to chain upgrades sequentially, so each node is fully back before the next one starts:

<!--Start PulumiCodeChooser -->
```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as talos from "@pulumiverse/talos";

const cp0 = new talos.machine.Machine("cp0", {
    node: "10.5.0.1",
    image: "ghcr.io/siderolabs/installer:v1.10.0",
    drainOnUpgrade: true,
});
// ...
const cp1 = new talos.machine.Machine("cp1", {
    node: "10.5.0.2",
    image: "ghcr.io/siderolabs/installer:v1.10.0",
    drainOnUpgrade: true,
}, {
    dependsOn: [cp0],
});
// ...
